#: ../doc/agent_cli.rst:6
msgid "Command Line Interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/agent_cli.rst:8
msgid "Bring OpenShot into your command-line workflow. Import footage, trim and arrange clips, apply effects, animate properties with keyframes, and export videos from your terminal. Use a few commands to automate repetitive edits, write a script for a recurring project, or let an AI agent help assemble and refine a video."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/agent_cli.rst:13
msgid "The command line works with the same projects as the editor. You can control an open editor and review changes as you go, or work in a **headless session** without opening a window. A session keeps your project open between commands, including its edits, undo history, and export jobs. Save it as an ``.osp`` project whenever you want to continue editing later."
msgstr ""

