#: ../doc/agent_cli.rst:127
msgid "Working with scripts and AI agents"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/agent_cli.rst:129
msgid "AI coding agents such as **Codex** and **Claude Code** can use the CLI to inspect and edit OpenShot projects through terminal commands. Give your agent the path to your OpenShot executable, the media or project to work with, and the desired result: duration, dimensions, animation style, and output location. Ask it to read ``--cli intro`` before starting. The same commands work when you type them yourself or run them from a script."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/agent_cli.rst:136
msgid "Start with ``intro``, then use command-specific help as needed. A useful workflow is to select a session, inspect the project, make a small set of changes, review the result, and save. Commands return structured JSON so scripts and agents can use object IDs and results directly instead of interpreting screen output."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/agent_cli.rst:141
msgid "**Inspect before editing.** Use returned IDs and property information instead of guessing names, track numbers, or timing. Select a session explicitly when more than one project is open."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/agent_cli.rst:144
msgid "**Group repeated edits.** Use ``edit apply`` for a sequence of changes or ``edit bulk`` to apply a template to selected clips. Validate with ``--dry-run`` before applying a batch."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/agent_cli.rst:147
msgid "**Check animation.** Choose a coordinate space, start with a few keyframes, and use easing presets for familiar motion. ``keyframe preview`` samples the curve so you can spot pauses or jumps before exporting. Review rendered motion as well; a contact sheet alone cannot show how an animation feels."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/agent_cli.rst:151
msgid "**Save and follow exports.** Save the project explicitly and check the export job's status before treating an output as complete. If a request times out, inspect its status before repeating an edit."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/agent_cli.rst:155
msgid "The sections below explain these workflows and their timing conventions."
msgstr ""

