msgid "On a desktop, ``session show`` creates the editor in the same process and keeps the live project, IDs, history, export jobs, and connection. Repeated calls raise the existing window. ``session start --show`` opens it immediately. Sessions started without a display, or with ``QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen``/``minimal``, cannot later show a desktop window. For those sessions, save and open the project in a new desktop session. Once shown, close the session through the editor window."
